<header><p class="enc-kicker">Historical factor</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fiscal crisis</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fiscal crisis refers to a state's inability to raise enough revenue to meet its military and administrative costs, often leading to debasement, heavier taxation, unpaid troops and revolt. It was a recurring cause of decline, seen in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a>'s repeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereign-default">bankruptcies</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming Empire</a>'s collapse, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>'s later debts and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a>'s overstretch.</p></div>
